From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Apex <apex@localhost>
Date: Wed, 24 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] elan: Recover from a dark frame on 04f3:0c6e

elan_save_img_frame() rejects a frame that is darker than the
background at every pixel. That happens when the background was taken
with a finger on the sensor. CAPTURE_CHECK_ENOUGH_FRAMES then fails the
whole session with a message-less FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL ("unspecified
error" in fprintd). The 0x0c6e sits in an ASUS power key, so a finger
often rests on it while calibration takes the background.

Turning the error into a retry at the end of the capture is not enough.
stop_capture_complete() reports finger-off without asking the sensor,
and the next AWAIT_FINGER_ON (enroll), or fprintd's restart of the
identify, calibrates about 1 ms later. The new background is taken with
the same finger on the sensor, the next frame is dark again, and a
resting finger turns into a loop of retries, each only a few USB
transfers long.

So for ELAN_RETRY_ON_DARK_FRAME devices (0x0c6e):

- Report FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER at the first dark frame, while
  the finger is still there, and drop all frames of that capture.
- Keep the capture running until the finger is lifted, the same way it
  runs after a good frame: pre_scan_cmd with ELAN_FINGER_TIMEOUT, and for
  each 0x55 the frame is read and dropped. Polls are
  ELAN_DARK_FRAME_POLL_DELAY (50 ms) apart. The capture ends when the
  read times out, when the sensor answers 0x00 or 0xaf (the 0002 lift
  semantics, which now also take a dark frame as proof of a finger), or
  ELAN_DARK_FRAME_LIFT_TIMEOUT (10 s) after the dark frame. Only then is
  stop_cmd sent and finger-off reported, so the next calibration
  normally takes its background without the finger.
- Allow at most ELAN_DARK_FRAME_MAX_RETRIES (3) consecutive captures to
  end this way. The next dark frame fails the session with
  FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL, as before. A capture that ends without a dark
  frame resets the count, which survives fprintd's restarts of the
  identify.

A finger that is never lifted therefore gives three prompts, 10 s apart,
and then the stock error.

Apex carries this patch but does not enable it. Enable it only when a
debug log from the sensor shows
  frame darker than background; finger present during calibration?
followed by the session error.

New debug lines, for example:
  frame darker than background: asking to remove the finger (retry 1 of 3)
  finger still present after the dark frame: frame dropped
  finger still present 10000 ms after the dark frame: ending capture
  capture after a dark frame ended; the next one calibrates again
  frame darker than background in 4 captures in a row: giving up

Applies on top of the Apex patches 0001 and 0002.
---
 libfprint/drivers/elan.c |   97 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 libfprint/drivers/elan.h |   20 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 113 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
index 03576d568acb..3be6ad716b43 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
@@ -89,6 +89,15 @@ struct _FpiDeviceElan
    * elan_dev_reset_state (), which starts every capture */
   unsigned int    transient_retries;
   gint64          transient_start;
+  /* ELAN_RETRY_ON_DARK_FRAME: a frame of this capture was darker than the
+   * background, and the capture now waits for the finger to be lifted;
+   * dark_frame_start is the monotonic time (us) of that frame */
+  gboolean        dark_frame;
+  gint64          dark_frame_start;
+  /* consecutive captures that ended on a dark frame: counted in
+   * elan_dark_frame (), cleared in dev_init () and by a capture without a dark
+   * frame, and kept by elan_dev_reset_state () */
+  unsigned int    dark_frame_retries;
   /* end state */
 };
 G_DEFINE_TYPE (FpiDeviceElan, fpi_device_elan, FP_TYPE_IMAGE_DEVICE);
@@ -110,6 +119,8 @@ elan_dev_reset_state (FpiDeviceElan *elandev)
   elandev->calib_status = 0;
   elandev->transient_retries = 0;
   elandev->transient_start = 0;
+  elandev->dark_frame = FALSE;
+  elandev->dark_frame_start = 0;
 
   g_free (elandev->last_read);
   elandev->last_read = NULL;
@@ -567,7 +578,9 @@ elan_transient_status (FpiSsm *ssm, FpiDeviceElan *self)
   gint64 elapsed_ms;
   int delay_ms;
 
-  if ((self->dev_type & ELAN_TRANSIENT_STATUS_LIFT) && self->num_frames > 0)
+  /* a dark frame also means that a finger was present */
+  if ((self->dev_type & ELAN_TRANSIENT_STATUS_LIFT) &&
+      (self->num_frames > 0 || self->dark_frame))
     {
       fp_dbg ("pre-scan status 0x%02x after %d frames: finger lifted",
               self->last_read[0], self->num_frames);
@@ -602,6 +615,68 @@ elan_transient_status (FpiSsm *ssm, FpiDeviceElan *self)
   fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed (ssm, CAPTURE_WAIT_FINGER, delay_ms);
 }
 
+/* Handle a frame darker than the background on a device in
+ * ELAN_RETRY_ON_DARK_FRAME, and every frame read after it in the same
+ * capture. Calls exactly one of fpi_ssm_mark_failed (),
+ * fpi_ssm_mark_completed () and fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed ().
+ *
+ * Calibration takes the background right before the capture, so a dark
+ * frame means that the finger was on the sensor already then. On the first
+ * dark frame, FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER is reported at once, while the
+ * finger is still there. The session fails with FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL
+ * instead, as on other devices, when ELAN_DARK_FRAME_MAX_RETRIES
+ * consecutive captures have already ended on a dark frame.
+ *
+ * Finger-off is reported, and the next calibration starts, only when this
+ * capture ends. So the capture goes on until the finger is lifted, as it
+ * would after a good frame: pre_scan_cmd with ELAN_FINGER_TIMEOUT, sent
+ * ELAN_DARK_FRAME_POLL_DELAY after the previous frame. A 0x55 means the
+ * finger is still there; its frame is read, dropped, and this function runs
+ * again. The capture ends when that read times out, when an
+ * ELAN_TRANSIENT_STATUS_LIFT device answers 0x00 or 0xaf, or at the latest
+ * ELAN_DARK_FRAME_LIFT_TIMEOUT after the dark frame. capture_complete () then
+ * reports nothing more.
+ *
+ * A pending delayed jump behaves on cancellation as described for
+ * elan_transient_status (). */
+static void
+elan_dark_frame (FpiSsm *ssm, FpiDeviceElan *self)
+{
+  gint64 now = g_get_monotonic_time ();
+
+  if (!self->dark_frame)
+    {
+      if (self->dark_frame_retries >= ELAN_DARK_FRAME_MAX_RETRIES)
+        {
+          fp_dbg ("frame darker than background in %u captures in a row: giving up",
+                  self->dark_frame_retries + 1);
+          fpi_ssm_mark_failed (ssm, fpi_device_error_new (FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL));
+          return;
+        }
+
+      self->dark_frame = TRUE;
+      self->dark_frame_start = now;
+      self->dark_frame_retries++;
+      fp_dbg ("frame darker than background: asking to remove the finger (retry %u of %d)",
+              self->dark_frame_retries, ELAN_DARK_FRAME_MAX_RETRIES);
+      fpi_image_device_retry_scan (FP_IMAGE_DEVICE (self), FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER);
+    }
+  else if (now - self->dark_frame_start >= (gint64) ELAN_DARK_FRAME_LIFT_TIMEOUT * 1000)
+    {
+      fp_dbg ("finger still present %d ms after the dark frame: ending capture",
+              ELAN_DARK_FRAME_LIFT_TIMEOUT);
+      fpi_ssm_mark_completed (ssm);
+      return;
+    }
+  else
+    {
+      fp_dbg ("finger still present after the dark frame: frame dropped");
+    }
+
+  self->cmd_timeout = ELAN_FINGER_TIMEOUT;
+  fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed (ssm, CAPTURE_WAIT_FINGER, ELAN_DARK_FRAME_POLL_DELAY);
+}
+
 static void
 capture_run_state (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
 {
@@ -650,8 +725,13 @@ capture_run_state (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
       break;
 
     case CAPTURE_CHECK_ENOUGH_FRAMES:
-      r = elan_save_img_frame (self);
-      if (r < 0)
+      /* after a dark frame, every frame is dropped */
+      r = self->dark_frame ? -1 : elan_save_img_frame (self);
+      if (r < 0 && (self->dev_type & ELAN_RETRY_ON_DARK_FRAME))
+        {
+          elan_dark_frame (ssm, self);
+        }
+      else if (r < 0)
         {
           fpi_ssm_mark_failed (ssm, fpi_device_error_new (FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL));
         }
@@ -682,7 +762,12 @@ capture_complete (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *_dev, GError *error)
       (g_error_matches (error, G_USB_DEVICE_ERROR, G_USB_DEVICE_ERROR_TIMED_OUT) &&
        fpi_ssm_get_cur_state (ssm) == CAPTURE_WAIT_FINGER))
     {
-      if (self->num_frames >= ELAN_MIN_FRAMES)
+      if (self->dark_frame)
+        {
+          /* the retry was reported at the dark frame */
+          fp_dbg ("capture after a dark frame ended; the next one calibrates again");
+        }
+      else if (self->num_frames >= ELAN_MIN_FRAMES)
         {
           elan_submit_image (dev);
         }
@@ -699,6 +784,9 @@ capture_complete (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *_dev, GError *error)
       fpi_image_device_session_error (dev, error);
     }
 
+  if (!self->dark_frame)
+    self->dark_frame_retries = 0;
+
   /* Note: We always stop capturing even if that may not be needed always.
    * Doing this between captures appears to make it at least less likely for
    * devices to end up in a bad state.
@@ -1010,6 +1098,7 @@ dev_init (FpImageDevice *dev)
   /* common params */
   self->dev_type = fpi_device_get_driver_data (FP_DEVICE (dev));
   self->background = NULL;
+  self->dark_frame_retries = 0;
   self->process_frame = elan_process_frame_thirds;
 
   switch (self->dev_type)
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.h b/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
index 1e866f62c5fb..74e435a65657 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
@@ -61,6 +61,26 @@
  * so an idle sensor that keeps answering cannot poll at 100 Hz. */
 #define ELAN_TRANSIENT_STATUS_BACKOFF ELAN_0C6E
 
+/* press sensors (0x0c6e sits in an ASUS power key) are often touched while
+ * calibration takes the background. On these devices a frame darker than
+ * that background does not fail the session with FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL.
+ * FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER is reported at once, and the capture waits
+ * for the finger to be lifted before it ends, so that the next calibration
+ * does not take its background with the finger still on the sensor (see
+ * elan_dark_frame ()). */
+#define ELAN_RETRY_ON_DARK_FRAME ELAN_0C6E
+
+/* ELAN_RETRY_ON_DARK_FRAME: the longest wait for the lift after a dark
+ * frame, and the delay between two pre-scan polls while the finger is still
+ * present (ms) */
+#define ELAN_DARK_FRAME_LIFT_TIMEOUT ELAN_CMD_TIMEOUT
+#define ELAN_DARK_FRAME_POLL_DELAY 50
+
+/* ELAN_RETRY_ON_DARK_FRAME: consecutive captures that may end on a dark frame
+ * with a retry. The next dark frame fails the session with
+ * FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL, as on other devices. */
+#define ELAN_DARK_FRAME_MAX_RETRIES 3
+
 /* min FW version that supports calibration */
 #define ELAN_MIN_CALIBRATION_FW 0x0138
 
-- 
2.53.0

